  "gaps": [
    "The student's chosen concentration is not known; the 15-semester-hour concentration block is recorded as a single requirement. Options are General (ISSC343, ITMG481, INFO222, ISSC368, ISSC456), Critical Infrastructure (HLSS310, ISSC477, ISSC478, ISSC479, ISSC480), Digital Forensics (ISSC455, ISSC456, ISSC457, ISSC458, ISSC459), Privacy and Surveillance (INTL305, ISSC473, ISSC474, ISSC475, ISSC476), and Wireless and Mobile Security (ISSC412, ISSC415, ISSC442, ISSC456, ISSC457), each 3 semester hours.",
    "The capture does not state a residency or institutional-credit requirement, or which requirements must be completed at the school.",
    "The capture does not state transfer credit limits.",
    "ISSC499 prerequisite: completion of a minimum of 106 hours toward the program, including ENGL101 or ENGL110; it should be taken as the last course before graduation. This is a sequencing rule, not a credit requirement.",
    "Footnote markers 1 (Arts & Humanities) and 2 (ISSC499) are not explicitly linked to their notes in the capture. The notes appear to be the literature-course prerequisite (ENGL101 or ENGL110) and the ISSC499 prerequisite."
  ],
